  "notes": "The only real filter is `type == \"release\"` (line 386) -- the two real snapshot entries (\"26.3-snapshot-9\", \"26.3-snapshot-8\") and both real old_alpha entries (\"rd-132328\", \"rd-132211\") are dropped. The one thing worth flagging precisely: unlike Purpur and Paper, `listVersions()` never sorts its result (ServerJarProviders.swift:385-388 is a bare filter+compactMap+map, no `.sorted`) -- the returned order is exactly Mojang's own manifest order, which happens to already be newest-first in this real response but is not guaranteed to be by anything this function does. A Rust port that reuses one shared \"sort every provider's list\" helper would silently change Vanilla's contract.",
